WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.060
Hello, my name is Zisl Slepovitch

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.603
and I'm musician in residence at Yale

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.079
University's Fortunoff Video Archive

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.730
for Holocaust Testimonies.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.069
This video series is designed as a

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.491
companion to our album, Where

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.239
Is Our Homeland, which is the first

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.340
volume in the archives' ongoing effort

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.620
to present songs and poems

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.583
performed by survivors in testimonies

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:57.699
given to the Fortunoff Archive

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.670
over the last 40 years.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.779
You can learn more about the project

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.130
on the Archive's website

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.460
songsfromtestimonies.org.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.049
Where Is Our Homeland?

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.309
Songs from Testimonies.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.489
Volume One was recorded in 2019

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.499
by the Zisl Slepovitch Ensemble,

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.229
featuring renowned singer Sasha

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.879
Lurje, Craig Judelman on

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.350
the violin, Joshua Camp on the

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.109
accordion, keyboards and guitar,

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.329
Dmitry Ishenko on the bass,

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.980
and myself on woodwinds.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.529
The songs in this collection differ

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.098
vastly in terms of style, social

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:33.645
and historical background, language

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.589
and many other aspects.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.749
But collectively they create

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.669
a multidimensional picture of

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.829
Jewish life before and during

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:42.830
World War II.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.674
In this episode, we're going to talk

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.019
about and listen to another

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.840
song from Liubov' K.'s

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.040
testimony "Tuchi nad

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.100
Budishchem Vstali," "The

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.140
Clouds Gather Over Budishchem."

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.419
It is noteworthy that the entire

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.519
Fortunoff Video Archive music

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.310
project started in 2018

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.500
with Liubov's testimony.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.499
With the Zisl Slepovitch Ensemble,

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.290
featuring the wonderful and

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.012
world-renowned singer Sasha Lurje,

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.619
we have recorded two albums,

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.780
26 songs in total,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.960
and I'm preparing two other volumes

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.260
to be recorded

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.667
with really fascinating

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.190
and unique repertoire.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.340
"Tuchi nad Budishchem Vstali"

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.900
is a retexting

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.410
and melodic adaptation

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.959
of Pavel Armand's music

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.840
and lyrics for the song "Tuchi

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:43.150
nad gorodom Vstali,"

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.890
"The Clouds Gathered Over the City,"

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.359
performed by the popular Soviet

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.389
actor and singer Mark

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.414
Bernes in the Sergei

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.650
Yutkevich's 1938

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.690
film Chelovek s Ruzhyom,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.009
The Man With a Gun.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.100
The song quickly gained popularity.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.039
Arman's text conveys the heartbreak

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.657
of a young man who's going to the

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.330
war and is bidding farewell

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.309
to the young woman he loves.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.587
The labor camp version, shared by

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.499
Liubov', depicts the horrific

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.329
realities of slave labor,

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.480
hunger, cold, lack

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.590
of basic living facilities,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.019
and the cruelty of the Ukrainian

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.020
guard, Stepan.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.339
The song has the time and feel of

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.679
a waltz, one of the most popular

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.719
genres in the 1930s

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.219
Soviet urban culture.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.100
